### **Float Label Best Practices**

1. **Consistent Spacing**: Use `mb-6` class on the container div for consistent spacing between fields
2. **ID Matching**: Ensure the input/select `id` matches the label's `for` attribute
3. **Full Width**: Apply `class="w-full"` to form controls for consistent width
4. **Required Indicators**: Add asterisk (*) directly in the label text for required fields
5. **Validation Messages**: Place error messages below the float label using `p-message` component
6. **Disabled State**: Use `[disabled]="condition"` on the form control, not on the label
7. **Read-Only Inputs**: For display-only fields, use disabled text inputs instead of dropdowns

### **Float Label Anti-Patterns**

```html
<!-- ❌ WRONG - Placeholder on p-select with float label -->
<p-floatlabel variant="on">
  <p-select
    [placeholder]="'Select option' | translate"  <!-- ❌ Causes overlap -->
    [options]="options()"
  />
  <label>{{ 'label.option' | translate }}</label>
</p-floatlabel>

<!-- ❌ WRONG - Missing variant="on" -->
<p-floatlabel>  <!-- ❌ Should specify variant="on" -->
  <input pInputText id="name" />
  <label for="name">Name</label>
</p-floatlabel>

<!-- ❌ WRONG - Hardcoded text instead of translation keys -->
<p-floatlabel variant="on">
  <input pInputText id="name" />
  <label for="name">Name</label>  <!-- ❌ Use translation keys -->
</p-floatlabel>

<!-- ❌ WRONG - Mismatched id and for attributes -->
<p-floatlabel variant="on">
  <input pInputText id="userName" />
  <label for="name">{{ 'label.name' | translate }}</label>  <!-- ❌ IDs don't match -->
</p-floatlabel>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT - All best practices followed -->
<div class="mb-6">
  <p-floatlabel variant="on">
    <p-select
      id="status"
      formControlName="status"
      [options]="statusOptions()"
      optionLabel="name"
      optionValue="id"
      class="w-full"
